WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.441 --> 00:00:07.005
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> <b>PART 3</b>

2
00:00:10.492 --> 00:00:15.086
Some months later, Mrs Myers appeared in court.

3
00:00:16.031 --> 00:00:23.232
‘So, Mrs Myers,’ said the judge, ‘what’s all this with the cards?’

4
00:00:23.737 --> 00:00:26.767
‘I need to earn money,’ said the old lady.

5
00:00:26.816 --> 00:00:29.911
‘At my age, I’m not going to be a dancer!’

6
00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:36.819
‘Somebody complained that you are not reading the cards properly,’ said the judge.

7
00:00:37.258 --> 00:00:42.798
‘If they’re going to pay you a pound, people expect a proper reading.’

8
00:00:43.368 --> 00:00:47.555
‘But most people don’t complain,’ the old lady replied.

9
00:00:47.652 --> 00:00:53.077
‘I tell them things they want to hear. And sometimes I even get it right…’

10
00:00:53.273 --> 00:00:57.655
‘But,’ said the judge, ‘here we have a witness.

11
00:00:58.079 --> 00:01:01.435
Please tell us about it, Mrs McCleary.’

12
00:01:02.201 --> 00:01:06.713
‘Mrs Myers read the cards for me,’ said Mrs McCleary.

13
00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:11.731
‘She told me that in a year I’d be married, that my husband would be

14
00:01:11.747 --> 00:01:15.120
a rich young man and that we’d move abroad.’

15
00:01:15.494 --> 00:01:21.034
‘But Mrs McCleary is already married,’ said the judge.

16
00:01:22.288 --> 00:01:26.133
‘She married Inspector McCleary three years ago.

17
00:01:26.377 --> 00:01:30.548
So how do you explain this nonsense, Mrs Myers?’

18
00:01:31.313 --> 00:01:36.347
‘Well, she said she was single,’ said the old lady, calmly.

19
00:01:36.461 --> 00:01:40.909
‘So I predicted a wedding for her and a rich husband.’

20
00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:46.693
‘And what about the old man and the journey abroad?’ asked Mrs McCleary.

21
00:01:47.181 --> 00:01:51.156
‘For something more to say,’ replied Mrs Myers.

22
00:01:51.189 --> 00:01:55.555
‘For a pound you need to say more than just two things.’

23
00:01:57.689 --> 00:02:02.072
‘You are a fraud, Mrs Myers,’ said the judge.

24
00:02:02.316 --> 00:02:05.411
‘You must pay a fine of fifty pounds.

25
00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:07.871
I hope you learn your lesson.’